WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.100
- Today on "Drew," we're flashing back

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:05.390
to our favorite moments from Season One.

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:07.680
- "I have a date with Lisa!"
- "Lisa!" (screams)

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:10.220
Only Eddie Murphy could
get me literally rolling

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:14.270
on the floor, plus our
two-week premier event starts

00:00:14.270 --> 00:00:16.270
Monday from Hollywood.

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:18.420
We're revealing superstar guests,

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:20.750
like one of the most talented singers

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:23.900
in the world, Billie Eilish.

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:25.438
It all starts now!

00:00:25.438 --> 00:00:28.021
(upbeat music)

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:31.452
- [Announcer] Please
welcome Drew Barrymore!

00:00:31.452 --> 00:00:33.540
(audience cheers)

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:36.180
- Hello, everyone, Season Two

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:39.610
of our first show is just four days away.

00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:41.700
On Monday, September 13th,

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:45.880
we're kicking off a brand
new season full of surprises,

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:48.994
signature segments,
and yes, stain removal!

00:00:48.994 --> 00:00:50.160
(audience laughs)

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:53.810
The stain busting will
never stop, don't you worry!

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:56.440
All right, we're having a
big two-week premier event,

00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:59.690
paying homage to all of
our favorite hometowns,

00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:04.040
and that feeling that
there's no place like home?

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:07.400
Well, we're starting in my own town of LA

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:11.100
and we're ending up here
in our show's hometown

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:13.869
and my new hometown of New York City.

00:01:13.869 --> 00:01:15.169
(audience cheers)
I know!

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:19.420
I do heart New York.
(man laughs)

00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:21.950
This week, we're having a little pre-party

00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:25.100
and celebrating our favorite
moments from Season One.

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.930
Let's kick things off with a
guest who had some great advice

00:01:28.930 --> 00:01:32.780
about the importance of
celebrating ourselves,

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:34.660
and here's our very candid conversation

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:38.560
with the legendary, the hilarious,

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:42.700
and wise Eddie Murphy, take a look.

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:44.990
I was lucky enough

00:01:44.990 --> 00:01:48.950
to meet our first guest when
I was just seven years old.

00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:52.480
He was a couple of seasons
into his transformative run

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:54.270
on "Saturday Night Live,"

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:58.260
where he immortalized
characters like Mr. Robinson

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:03.130
and Gumby, but he was destined
for even greater things,

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:06.060
and he found them

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:10.280
as the star in some of the most
iconic comedies of all time.

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:12.560
Let's talk about "Trading Places."

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:15.970
Let's talk about "Beverly Hills Cop."

00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:19.820
Let's talk about "Coming to America."

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:23.140
And he still pursued
his first love, standup,

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:24.440
and released two specials,

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:28.730
including the highest-grossing
stand-up comedy concert film

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:30.310
of all time.

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:34.810
And then, the father of
10 gifted his talents

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:37.810
to beloved family films
that shaped generations,

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:40.120
voicing characters in films like "Mulan"

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:42.580
and the "Shrek" franchise.

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:45.280
And now after celebrated performances

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:48.280
in 2006's "Dream Girls"

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:51.580
and 2019's "Dolomite Is My Name,"

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:54.343
he is returning to his kingdom, Zamunda,

00:02:56.049 --> 00:02:58.430
as Prince Akeem in "Coming to America."

00:02:58.430 --> 00:03:01.409
This is one my very favorite
movies of all times.

00:03:01.409 --> 00:03:04.081
"I have a date with Lisa!"
(audience laughs)

00:03:04.081 --> 00:03:06.670
I can't believe I'm saying
this in front of the person.

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:10.574
Please welcome the one
of a kind Eddie Murphy.

00:03:10.574 --> 00:03:13.527
(audience cheers)

00:03:13.527 --> 00:03:15.027
- Thank you, that is so nice.

00:03:15.027 --> 00:03:19.599
You made me feel like I did
some good movies. (laughs)

00:03:19.599 --> 00:03:21.844
(audience laughs)
Hi, Drew Barrymore!

00:03:21.844 --> 00:03:24.104
- Hello, Eddie Murphy!

00:03:24.104 --> 00:03:26.400
I'm so happy to see you.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.353
- Yeah, happy to see you too.

00:03:28.353 --> 00:03:32.273
- I mean, 1982.
- You were just a little baby-

00:03:32.273 --> 00:03:33.263
- Yeah.
- When I met you.

00:03:33.263 --> 00:03:36.462
- And there we were.
- Just a little baby!

00:03:36.462 --> 00:03:39.086
(laughs) Aw!
- And look at you and I.

00:03:39.086 --> 00:03:41.670
- [Eddie] You're just a baby. (laughs)

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:44.340
I'm young, too, I think
I'm 19 or 20 there.

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:46.543
- Yeah.
- I remember Tim Kazurinsky.

00:03:47.630 --> 00:03:51.300
You guys were buddies that
week, became buddies with him.

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:53.120
- I did, I gravitated towards him.

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:56.090
He was so nice to me.
- Yeah, you guys were cute.

00:03:56.090 --> 00:04:00.900
- Do you remember doing the "E.T." sketch?

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:04.790
You were Mr. T looking for his boy, E,

00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:07.770
and I don't know if you remember this,

00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:09.950
but Steven Spielberg was there.

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:13.650
He was very protective of me
at that time, I was so lucky.

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:14.590
- You know what's so strange

00:04:14.590 --> 00:04:16.930
about that whole SNL experience?

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:18.133
It was so long ago,

00:04:19.630 --> 00:04:22.390
so sometimes there'll be a sketch on,

00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:23.880
and I won't even remember the sketch.

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:24.717
I'll be watching it, going,

00:04:24.717 --> 00:04:27.960
"What is this sketch, what happens next?"

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:29.760
It's so much, it's so long ago,

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:33.310
and so many sketches in
between that and so much stuff,

00:04:33.310 --> 00:04:35.028
a lot of times, I don't remember it.

00:04:35.028 --> 00:04:36.940
I don't remember that Mr. T sketch.

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:38.410
- I just remember everything

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:41.220
from that show very vividly, but I, too,

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:44.579
have surrealistic gaps.

00:04:44.579 --> 00:04:46.100
- Yeah, it's surreal.

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:47.940
Yeah, I can imagine.

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:49.960
You were a little baby when you started.

00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:52.466
- Well, and that was in 1982.
- You were just a baby.

00:04:52.466 --> 00:04:53.577
(Eddie laughs)
- I know,

00:04:53.577 --> 00:04:56.640
and you have 10 kids,
so I can only imagine

00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:59.640
what your perspective is now,
'cause I have two daughters,

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:01.690
and my perspective is
completely different now

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:02.786
than when I was seven.

00:05:02.786 --> 00:05:04.230
- No, I mean, a totally different,

00:05:04.230 --> 00:05:07.421
not just 10 kids, I have
my first grandchild now.

00:05:07.421 --> 00:05:08.475
(Drew gasps)

00:05:08.475 --> 00:05:12.440
- (squeals) Congratulations!
(audience applauds)

00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:15.394
- Now, I'm a Papa, she
calls me Papa. (laughs)

00:05:15.394 --> 00:05:18.640
- Oh, that's so wonderful.

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:20.590
I was reading that you said

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:22.820
your house is just a hub of activity

00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:27.710
and that you like to hear the
voices just all over the place

00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:29.280
and how proud you are of your kids,

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:32.665
and all 10 turned out
really wonderful people.

00:05:32.665 --> 00:05:36.030
- Yeah, my favorite thing of all is

00:05:36.030 --> 00:05:39.340
to have no schedule, have
nothing that I have to do,

00:05:39.340 --> 00:05:43.630
and I'm home and all my
kids and all their friends,

00:05:43.630 --> 00:05:47.490
they're all around, and I can
hear where everybody's at.

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:50.500
That's nirvana for me. (laughs)

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:51.520
- And I was reading

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:56.830
that you lean into
being a spiritual person

00:05:56.830 --> 00:06:00.060
and being centered,

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:03.850
and that you said maybe you
avoided some of the pitfalls

00:06:03.850 --> 00:06:07.960
that were so easy at your
disposal, if you will,

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:09.990
because of spirituality.

00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:12.090
Is that true?

00:06:12.090 --> 00:06:14.360
- Yeah, I'm very grounded spiritually,

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:16.650
and not so much in any religion,

00:06:16.650 --> 00:06:20.760
just a connection with God.

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:24.390
Being a young person in
this business, it's a lot.

00:06:24.390 --> 00:06:27.790
It's like you gotta navigate
through a minefield.

00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:31.850
There's so many ways you
could just destroy yourself.

00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:34.350
A lot of the people that I've seen

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:37.590
that destroyed themselves,
a lot of my contemporaries,

00:06:37.590 --> 00:06:41.490
are the people like Michael
and Prince and Whitney

00:06:41.490 --> 00:06:43.470
and people that came on the
scene around the same age

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:44.893
that I am.
- Yeah.

00:06:46.854 --> 00:06:49.633
- It was this self-destructive
thing that they had.

00:06:50.630 --> 00:06:53.850
That's my biggest blessing,
that I got started really early,

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:55.760
I knew what I wanted to
do really, really young,

00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:57.420
and that I love myself.

00:06:57.420 --> 00:07:00.643
I never hated myself, I
never beat up on myself.

00:07:03.527 --> 00:07:05.487
I've always been my biggest fan. (laughs)

00:07:05.487 --> 00:07:08.150
(audience laughs)

00:07:08.150 --> 00:07:11.260
- I love that, you deserve to be,

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:13.350
'cause we're all there with you.

00:07:13.350 --> 00:07:17.550
What would you say to
someone who does struggle

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:20.340
with, call it self-love?

00:07:20.340 --> 00:07:25.050
I'm asking for myself, 'cause
I love and respect myself,

00:07:25.050 --> 00:07:26.780
but I fall off the wagon

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:28.281
with total (laughs) self-flagellation

00:07:28.281 --> 00:07:32.930
and being too hard and not
meeting my own expectations.

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:34.861
Do you have any advice for me?

00:07:34.861 --> 00:07:36.690
- It's an inward search

00:07:38.300 --> 00:07:41.810
and it's personal and it's
just between you and you,

00:07:41.810 --> 00:07:43.393
and the outside stuff,

00:07:48.090 --> 00:07:51.440
I don't let anything
that's not constructive,

00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:53.490
I don't let anything negative in.

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:56.320
You have to train yourself
to turn away from it.

00:07:56.320 --> 00:08:00.260
When negative stuff comes in,
stuff that's not constructive,

00:08:00.260 --> 00:08:02.110
you have to turn from it.

00:08:02.110 --> 00:08:05.110
You're here, and then you're blessed.

00:08:05.110 --> 00:08:06.890
You're here and you're blessed?

00:08:06.890 --> 00:08:08.370
You already won,

00:08:08.370 --> 00:08:12.160
so the negative energy,
there's no time for that.

00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:13.843
You won already.

00:08:13.843 --> 00:08:15.470
You know what you should do every morning?

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:16.900
- What?
- You should do

00:08:16.900 --> 00:08:18.363
a victory dance, you should
wake up every morning

00:08:18.363 --> 00:08:20.507
and do the Drew Barrymore victory dance.

00:08:20.507 --> 00:08:21.780
(everyone laughs)
"I won!"

00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:26.860
You've won, mama.

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:30.750
- I feel like the world's
biggest winner right now

00:08:30.750 --> 00:08:33.580
to hear such salient advice

00:08:33.580 --> 00:08:37.590
from someone I have respected
so much my whole life,

00:08:37.590 --> 00:08:42.480
and in 1982, when we did
"Saturday Night Live" together,

00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:44.677
then you had done "48 Hours,"

00:08:44.677 --> 00:08:48.773
"Trading Places," "Beverly
Hills Cop," by the way.

00:08:48.773 --> 00:08:51.630
- And "Delirious" right
in the middle of that.

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:53.767
The red leather suit is right
in the middle of that stuff.

00:08:53.767 --> 00:08:56.840
- [Drew] And at what exact point was "Raw"

00:08:56.840 --> 00:08:58.697
to that?
- Right after "Coming

00:08:58.697 --> 00:09:01.650
"to America" is "Raw."
- Oh, yeah, so that's '87.

00:09:01.650 --> 00:09:03.339
- I can tell, 'cause I have a perm.

00:09:03.339 --> 00:09:05.239
(audience laughs)
(laughs) That hair.

00:09:06.280 --> 00:09:10.450
- You had such a succession
of these epic films.

00:09:10.450 --> 00:09:11.980
You're so young.

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:16.160
Do you ever come down
from those periods of time

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:17.820
where you have hit after hit after hit

00:09:17.820 --> 00:09:19.710
and you're working, working, working?

00:09:19.710 --> 00:09:21.673
- I'll tell you what happened to me.

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:25.680
I had it all the way together
for years and years and years,

00:09:25.680 --> 00:09:28.340
and then what happened with movies is

00:09:28.340 --> 00:09:31.750
they started offering you
so much money to do stuff

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:34.150
that I wound up doing all,
you know what that's like?

00:09:34.150 --> 00:09:34.983
You would just do it and be like,

00:09:34.983 --> 00:09:37.741
"Hey, you wanna give me that
much money to do that (beep)?"

00:09:37.741 --> 00:09:40.820
"Okay."
(everyone laughs)

00:09:40.820 --> 00:09:43.823
A bunch of movies like
that, and it's forever.

00:09:43.823 --> 00:09:45.830
(laughs) Way after the money is spent,

00:09:45.830 --> 00:09:48.927
that (beep) movie is still
playing on a movie channel.

00:09:48.927 --> 00:09:52.060
(laughs) So I got to
where I stopped having

00:09:52.060 --> 00:09:53.160
fun making movies,

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:56.530
so I had to take a time off.

00:09:56.530 --> 00:09:59.113
In 2011, I think it was,

00:10:00.689 --> 00:10:03.190
I stopped for eight years.

00:10:03.190 --> 00:10:05.360
I just stopped making movies,

00:10:05.360 --> 00:10:08.020
and that's where I had
really, really quiet time

00:10:08.020 --> 00:10:09.330
and got re-centered

00:10:10.210 --> 00:10:12.420
to where if I'm gonna be doing something,

00:10:12.420 --> 00:10:14.813
I wanna be doing it because I wanna do it,

00:10:15.852 --> 00:10:19.000
and I got it all back together that way.

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:20.950
- That is the perfect
answer to that question,

00:10:20.950 --> 00:10:25.530
and the reason I asked is
because, since that 1982 time,

00:10:25.530 --> 00:10:28.130
and I had even been working
before that and so had you,

00:10:28.130 --> 00:10:30.720
but we're still here, we're still going.

00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:33.657
It's 30, 40 years later.
- That's what I said.

00:10:33.657 --> 00:10:34.717
That's why I said you should do

00:10:34.717 --> 00:10:36.730
the victory dance, how about this?

00:10:36.730 --> 00:10:39.943
We're in the business, Drew,
where people come and go.

00:10:41.190 --> 00:10:44.363
Every five years, there's a
brand new bunch of new faces,

00:10:45.735 --> 00:10:47.530
and anybody that's in this business

00:10:47.530 --> 00:10:50.070
for as long as you've
been in this business,

00:10:50.070 --> 00:10:51.850
as long as I've been in this business,

00:10:51.850 --> 00:10:55.159
I think that means that we're not stinky.

00:10:55.159 --> 00:10:58.120
(everybody laughs)

00:10:58.120 --> 00:11:00.840
It's been firmly established
that we are not stinky.

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:04.370
(audience applauds)
- It was very special advice

00:11:04.370 --> 00:11:05.820
to hear from Eddie,

00:11:05.820 --> 00:11:08.520
and the truth is I still
forget it all the time.

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:11.710
I need to write it on my
wall because he's right.

00:11:11.710 --> 00:11:15.870
We don't feel like we
have accomplished enough

00:11:15.870 --> 00:11:18.420
or that we're there at those goal lines.

00:11:18.420 --> 00:11:19.950
We (pounding fist) push and push and push

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:22.230
and really take ourselves down,

00:11:22.230 --> 00:11:24.960
and we need to lift
ourselves up, all right?

00:11:24.960 --> 00:11:28.220
I love that advice from Eddie.

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:31.870
All right, now sit tight because
we're just getting started.

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:36.260
There's more Eddie Murphy
and behind-the-scenes tidbits

00:11:36.260 --> 00:11:39.265
to his famous films in just a minute.

00:11:39.265 --> 00:11:40.098
(upbeat music)
We'll be right back.

00:11:40.098 --> 00:11:42.931
(audience cheers)

00:11:45.938 --> 00:11:48.539
- "I have a date with Lisa,"
will you say it with me?

00:11:48.539 --> 00:11:49.718
- Or how about I say it like this?

00:11:49.718 --> 00:11:51.074
"I have a date with Lisa?"

00:11:51.074 --> 00:11:52.212
No, I'll do it the right way.
- "I have a," I know, I-

00:11:52.212 --> 00:11:54.096
- "I have a date with Lisa!"
- "Lisa!" (screams)

00:11:54.096 --> 00:11:59.096
(audience cheers)
(Eddie laughs)

00:11:59.128 --> 00:12:01.100
- Now if I'd known you
was gonna roll around,

00:12:01.100 --> 00:12:02.092
I'd have did it the first time.

00:12:02.092 --> 00:12:03.515
(Drew laughs)
(audience laughs)

00:12:03.515 --> 00:12:06.098
(upbeat music)

00:12:07.475 --> 00:12:12.068
♪ If you're into fashion
or easy home decor ♪

00:12:12.068 --> 00:12:14.369
♪ New favorite recipes ♪

00:12:14.369 --> 00:12:16.768
♪ Plus fun celebrities ♪
(celebrities laugh)

00:12:16.768 --> 00:12:19.000
♪ Need a little good news ♪

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:21.233
- We're back to bring you more.

00:12:21.233 --> 00:12:23.517
♪ Barrymore ♪

00:12:23.517 --> 00:12:25.834
♪ Drew's all new for Season Two, yeah ♪

00:12:25.834 --> 00:12:28.105
♪ Barrymore ♪

00:12:28.105 --> 00:12:30.474
♪ Life improving, stain removing ♪

00:12:30.474 --> 00:12:33.150
♪ Barrymore ♪

00:12:33.150 --> 00:12:33.983
- [Announcer] The new season

00:12:33.983 --> 00:12:35.910
of "Drew" premieres September 13th.

00:12:39.926 --> 00:12:42.035
(upbeat music)

00:12:42.035 --> 00:12:45.090
(audience applauds)
- Welcome back.

00:12:45.090 --> 00:12:47.740
We're checking out some of
the most memorable moments

00:12:47.740 --> 00:12:50.167
from Season One, curated just for you,

00:12:50.167 --> 00:12:51.400
of "The Drew Barrymore Show,"

00:12:51.400 --> 00:12:54.380
with bonus director's cut commentary

00:12:54.380 --> 00:12:58.630
from someone with a unique
firsthand perspective, me.

00:12:58.630 --> 00:13:02.470
Now let's jump back into our
conversation with Eddie Murphy,

00:13:02.470 --> 00:13:06.220
where I may or may not
have gotten him to do

00:13:06.220 --> 00:13:10.250
one of my favorite lines
that I say every day

00:13:10.250 --> 00:13:13.210
from "Coming to America!"

00:13:13.210 --> 00:13:15.873
Okay, spoiler alert, I did, take a look!

00:13:16.780 --> 00:13:18.567
One of my favorite movies of all time is

00:13:18.567 --> 00:13:20.077
"Coming to America."

00:13:20.077 --> 00:13:25.000
"Coming to America 2" is here,

00:13:25.000 --> 00:13:28.220
and we can all finally go back to Zamunda.

00:13:28.220 --> 00:13:30.307
Was there a moment where you said,

00:13:30.307 --> 00:13:33.700
"Now is the right time
to make this sequel?"

00:13:33.700 --> 00:13:36.140
- No, it happened organically, this movie,

00:13:36.140 --> 00:13:39.060
the way it came together,
because the way the story ended,

00:13:39.060 --> 00:13:43.120
it was, "And they live
happily ever after,"

00:13:43.120 --> 00:13:44.940
and we didn't even think
about making a sequel,

00:13:44.940 --> 00:13:48.440
but then the movie became a cult movie.

00:13:48.440 --> 00:13:51.160
Little stuff from the
movie just stayed around.

00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:53.460
Of all the movies that I've done,

00:13:53.460 --> 00:13:56.110
no movie is on TV as much
as "Coming to America."

00:13:56.110 --> 00:13:59.270
It's always on and little
lines from the movie,

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:00.640
and, "Sexual Chocolate!"
(audience laughs)

00:14:00.640 --> 00:14:01.473
People say (laughs) that, little lines-

00:14:01.473 --> 00:14:02.700
- Definitely.
- From the movie,

00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:04.543
or the mic drop that everybody does.

00:14:05.620 --> 00:14:08.290
The very first mic drop
ever is Randy Watson

00:14:08.290 --> 00:14:09.657
from "Coming to America,"

00:14:10.600 --> 00:14:12.090
all this little stuff from the movie.

00:14:12.090 --> 00:14:15.053
And then what happened,
about 10 years ago,

00:14:16.470 --> 00:14:19.330
some people on Halloween would
dress up as the characters,

00:14:19.330 --> 00:14:22.090
and there's a restaurant in LA

00:14:22.090 --> 00:14:25.840
that, on Halloween, it
changes itself into McDowell's

00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:27.400
and they have a McDowell's menu,

00:14:27.400 --> 00:14:29.830
so it really is this cult movie.

00:14:29.830 --> 00:14:34.310
So it became that, and that's
when I started having the idea

00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:36.140
of, hey, well, the people
that really, really like

00:14:36.140 --> 00:14:39.910
that movie might wanna see a sequel to it.

00:14:39.910 --> 00:14:42.660
And then, when we figured
out a way to connect the dots

00:14:42.660 --> 00:14:47.050
and to make it make sense,
then we wrote a script

00:14:47.050 --> 00:14:48.460
and it came together right.

00:14:48.460 --> 00:14:50.970
- Can I ask a burning question

00:14:50.970 --> 00:14:53.370
that I've wondered ever
since I first saw the movie,

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:55.600
which is the little
child on the skateboard,

00:14:55.600 --> 00:14:57.670
because they've all taken the suitcases

00:14:57.670 --> 00:15:01.840
and they're wearing all
the fabulous Zamunda garb,

00:15:01.840 --> 00:15:05.667
was it like, "Let's just say
that we have so much clothes

00:15:05.667 --> 00:15:08.327
"that there are child's
sizes," or, "Screw it.

00:15:08.327 --> 00:15:11.360
"Tailor it, it's funnier?"
- No, we were taking

00:15:11.360 --> 00:15:14.310
license there, 'cause I
know it's (laughs) a kid

00:15:14.310 --> 00:15:17.190
and he has on a child's size.
(audience laughs)

00:15:17.190 --> 00:15:20.060
You have to remember, now,
the movie was a comedy,

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:23.603
and it was directed by
the great John Landis.

00:15:25.150 --> 00:15:28.120
People, when they talk
about "Coming to America,"

00:15:28.120 --> 00:15:29.530
when I'm asked about "Coming to America,"

00:15:29.530 --> 00:15:31.640
they get me and Arsenio,

00:15:31.640 --> 00:15:34.380
the actors that get all
the credit for the movie,

00:15:34.380 --> 00:15:35.770
and that movie is

00:15:37.710 --> 00:15:39.780
more John Landis than anything.

00:15:39.780 --> 00:15:41.270
And that's a John Landis joke,

00:15:41.270 --> 00:15:43.253
to have the kid go skating by.

00:15:44.417 --> 00:15:45.250
In the moment, he probably was like,

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:47.207
"Hey, have a kid skateboard by there."

00:15:47.207 --> 00:15:49.710
(laughs) He's like that.

00:15:49.710 --> 00:15:53.040
- It's my favorite moment,
other than, of course,

00:15:53.040 --> 00:15:56.120
the quote of, "I have a date with Lisa,"

00:15:56.120 --> 00:15:59.000
and I say it every day

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:01.650
because it's my version
of showing that I'm happy.

00:16:01.650 --> 00:16:03.856
- Aw, that's wonderful.

00:16:03.856 --> 00:16:06.500
- (laughs) Oh, we have the clip!

00:16:06.500 --> 00:16:07.833
May we show it, please?

00:16:11.420 --> 00:16:13.359
- I have a date with Lisa!

00:16:13.359 --> 00:16:15.109
Isn't that wonderful?

00:16:16.314 --> 00:16:19.460
(audience laughs)
(audience applauds)

00:16:19.460 --> 00:16:20.893
- That scene right there,

00:16:22.170 --> 00:16:25.060
the little girls that are in that scene,

00:16:25.060 --> 00:16:27.740
was a friend of mine named Jeffrey Moore

00:16:27.740 --> 00:16:31.360
who lived in Brooklyn, and he
stopped by the set that day,

00:16:31.360 --> 00:16:34.470
and the little girl in
the light blue jacket,

00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:36.230
that was his daughter and
she was just with him.

00:16:36.230 --> 00:16:38.100
We just put her in the scene
(snaps fingers) right there.

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:39.830
It just happened at that moment.

00:16:39.830 --> 00:16:42.421
- Would you ever say it with
me, will you say it with me?

00:16:42.421 --> 00:16:43.922
- Or how about I say it like this?

00:16:43.922 --> 00:16:45.907
(laughs) "I have a date with Lisa."

00:16:45.907 --> 00:16:50.061
(everybody laughs)
"I have a date with Lisa?"

00:16:50.061 --> 00:16:51.546
No, I'll do it the right way.
- "I have a," I know, I-

00:16:51.546 --> 00:16:53.265
- "I have a date with Lisa!"
- "Lisa!" (screams)

00:16:53.265 --> 00:16:58.265
(audience cheers)
(Eddie laughs)

00:17:00.254 --> 00:17:01.779
- Now if I'd known you
was gonna roll around,

00:17:01.779 --> 00:17:02.956
I'd have did it the first time.

00:17:02.956 --> 00:17:06.280
(Drew laughs)
(audience laughs)

00:17:06.280 --> 00:17:09.950
- Eddie, I'm so happy to see you.

00:17:09.950 --> 00:17:12.180
Thank you for giving me such incredible,

00:17:12.180 --> 00:17:13.800
salient life advice.

00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:16.670
- It's nice to see you,
too, and I look forward to,

00:17:16.670 --> 00:17:19.570
after all this pandemic stuff is over,

00:17:19.570 --> 00:17:22.262
come there and see you live in person.

00:17:22.262 --> 00:17:25.670
(Drew sighs)
(audience cheers)

00:17:25.670 --> 00:17:28.410
- I will roll myself up
in this carpet for you.

00:17:28.410 --> 00:17:29.830
I'll be a burrito
(Eddie laughs)

00:17:29.830 --> 00:17:34.600
by the time we finish, and I
will dance that victory dance

00:17:34.600 --> 00:17:38.406
and recognize the purpose.

00:17:38.406 --> 00:17:41.820
- Even if you don't do
it physically, get right.

00:17:41.820 --> 00:17:44.327
Always start the day
with, "I've already won.

00:17:44.327 --> 00:17:46.570
"At this game, I've already won."

00:17:46.570 --> 00:17:50.680
Now it's just about getting
the most out of everything,

00:17:50.680 --> 00:17:54.420
being here and your
babies and your family.

00:17:54.420 --> 00:17:57.330
- I very much recognize
that, and I love it coming

00:17:57.330 --> 00:18:01.520
from the person who has
made life make sense

00:18:01.520 --> 00:18:04.530
for so many of us on this planet

00:18:04.530 --> 00:18:08.090
by helping us love and
laugh and enjoy life

00:18:08.090 --> 00:18:11.550
and fall in love with the
extraordinary characters

00:18:11.550 --> 00:18:14.030
that are you that you've
put out into the world.

00:18:14.030 --> 00:18:15.255
Thank you.
- Thank you so much.

00:18:15.255 --> 00:18:17.142
(audience cheers)

00:18:17.142 --> 00:18:19.180
- (exclaims) Only Eddie Murphy could get

00:18:19.180 --> 00:18:21.840
me literally rolling on the floor

00:18:21.840 --> 00:18:23.408
like the carpet was a burrito!

00:18:23.408 --> 00:18:24.810
(audience laughs)
All right,

00:18:24.810 --> 00:18:27.592
more of our favorite moments
when we return, don't move!

00:18:27.592 --> 00:18:32.592
(upbeat music)
(audience cheers)

