00:19:06.718 --> 00:19:09.301
(upbeat music)

00:19:10.910 --> 00:19:12.520
- Cookbooks are my obsession,

00:19:12.520 --> 00:19:16.160
and it turns out I'm
not alone, watch this!

00:19:16.160 --> 00:19:18.873
- My Cookbook Club is

00:19:18.873 --> 00:19:22.820
Ina Garten, Barefoot Contessa,
"Modern Comfort Food."

00:19:22.820 --> 00:19:27.470
It has everything you exactly
wanna be eating right now,

00:19:27.470 --> 00:19:30.530
and you might look up the best tomato soup

00:19:30.530 --> 00:19:32.090
with a grilled cheese,

00:19:32.090 --> 00:19:35.370
but Ina always makes it
that much easier to make

00:19:35.370 --> 00:19:37.630
and with an ingredient you
wouldn't have expected,

00:19:37.630 --> 00:19:41.830
so it's that much more
delicious, it is ideal!

00:19:41.830 --> 00:19:43.950
She does this chicken breast with orzo

00:19:43.950 --> 00:19:45.460
that I did on my pretend cooking show,

00:19:45.460 --> 00:19:47.220
and I've made my chicken breasts that way

00:19:47.220 --> 00:19:49.590
so many times since then,
and I made it last night,

00:19:49.590 --> 00:19:53.890
and my kids and I were just
like, "This is delicious,"

00:19:53.890 --> 00:19:55.670
and all the desserts,

00:19:55.670 --> 00:19:58.611
the way she does potatoes in
that cookbook, her veggies.

00:19:58.611 --> 00:20:02.340
Ina Garten, Barefoot Contessa,
"Modern Comfort Food,"

00:20:02.340 --> 00:20:04.050
favorite cookbook right now.

00:20:04.050 --> 00:20:06.976
- Thank you for joining in
my obsession with cookbooks.

00:20:06.976 --> 00:20:09.559
(upbeat music)

00:20:14.588 --> 00:20:16.928
(upbeat music)

00:20:16.928 --> 00:20:18.470
(audience applauds)
- Welcome back

00:20:18.470 --> 00:20:20.640
to our Season Two pre-party.

00:20:20.640 --> 00:20:23.520
We're checking out some of our
favorite Season One moments

00:20:23.520 --> 00:20:26.070
and letting you in on
behind-the-scenes secrets

00:20:26.070 --> 00:20:29.380
ahead of our Season
Two premiere next week.

00:20:29.380 --> 00:20:32.430
One of my favorite parts of
this job is getting to meet

00:20:32.430 --> 00:20:37.080
so many incredible and inspiring
people from everywhere,

00:20:37.080 --> 00:20:40.880
and this person who's coming
up next really, really affected

00:20:40.880 --> 00:20:42.180
me, I love her.

00:20:42.180 --> 00:20:45.960
Debra Houston is a mother,
grandmother, great grandmother,

00:20:45.960 --> 00:20:49.730
and get this, the oldest
Soap Box Derby racer

00:20:49.730 --> 00:20:52.440
in the country, take a look.

00:20:52.440 --> 00:20:54.477
Here she is, it's Debra!

00:20:54.477 --> 00:20:56.547
(audience cheers)

00:20:56.547 --> 00:20:58.464
- Hi, Drew!
- Hi, Debra!

00:21:00.390 --> 00:21:02.413
I'm so excited to meet you.

00:21:03.370 --> 00:21:05.870
- And I'm excited to meet you, too!

00:21:05.870 --> 00:21:09.863
- How did you end up
getting into soapbox racing?

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:14.680
- Well, Indianapolis is
known for the racing,

00:21:14.680 --> 00:21:17.130
and a friend of mine had approached me

00:21:17.130 --> 00:21:21.500
about taking my grandchildren
to do the soapbox racing.

00:21:21.500 --> 00:21:25.610
And so I thought it would
be a good thing for them

00:21:25.610 --> 00:21:27.920
to get them off the computers,

00:21:27.920 --> 00:21:30.570
it'll teach them responsibility,

00:21:30.570 --> 00:21:33.720
and give them something
to do during the pandemic.

00:21:33.720 --> 00:21:36.370
So I took them to practice

00:21:36.370 --> 00:21:39.110
and they met their coach, Mr. Larry,

00:21:39.110 --> 00:21:42.880
and Mr. Larry kept
approaching me about racing.

00:21:42.880 --> 00:21:44.668
He said, "You're the perfect size.

00:21:44.668 --> 00:21:47.520
(audience laughs)
"You could fit in that car."

00:21:47.520 --> 00:21:50.290
He said, "Come on, do it,"
and I kept thinking about it

00:21:50.290 --> 00:21:51.617
and thinking about it, and I finally said,

00:21:51.617 --> 00:21:53.230
"Okay, I'll try it."
(audience applauds)

00:21:53.230 --> 00:21:56.030
- [Drew] I love it because, I mean,

00:21:56.030 --> 00:22:00.570
I learned that the oldest soapbox racer

00:22:00.570 --> 00:22:03.358
in your team is 14, right?

00:22:03.358 --> 00:22:05.460
(man laughing)
- Right.

00:22:05.460 --> 00:22:07.733
- I just love this!

00:22:07.733 --> 00:22:09.580
This is so cool!
(Debra laughs)

00:22:09.580 --> 00:22:12.460
Tiny, but mighty!
- Yes! (laughs)

00:22:12.460 --> 00:22:14.250
- What was going through your head

00:22:14.250 --> 00:22:15.783
the first time you were like-

00:22:16.980 --> 00:22:19.670
- Well, at first, I was a little nervous,

00:22:19.670 --> 00:22:22.840
and I was hyperventilating
because I was so nervous.

00:22:22.840 --> 00:22:26.740
And I went down that hill,

00:22:26.740 --> 00:22:30.771
and when I went down that hill,
I said, "Oh, I can do this,"

00:22:30.771 --> 00:22:34.230
and I started practicing and
kept going down that hill,

00:22:34.230 --> 00:22:36.163
and it turned out to be fun!

00:22:37.570 --> 00:22:39.800
At the same time, I was
going through chemo,

00:22:39.800 --> 00:22:44.177
so I said, "Well, rather than
sit up and worry about chemo,

00:22:44.177 --> 00:22:46.147
"I could be practicing and having fun

00:22:46.147 --> 00:22:49.330
"and just doing this
with my grandchildren,"

00:22:49.330 --> 00:22:52.560
and I really enjoyed it!
(audience applauds)

00:22:52.560 --> 00:22:54.600
- [Drew] And is it true

00:22:54.600 --> 00:22:58.910
that you're doing fantastically well now?

00:22:58.910 --> 00:23:01.239
- Yes, I am cancer-free.

00:23:01.239 --> 00:23:04.720
(Drew cheers)
(audience cheers)

00:23:04.720 --> 00:23:07.010
- Yes.
(Drew exclaims)

00:23:07.010 --> 00:23:09.350
- I asked that right
away when I found out,

00:23:09.350 --> 00:23:10.930
and it's just so important,

00:23:10.930 --> 00:23:13.680
and your story, your attitude,

00:23:13.680 --> 00:23:17.080
the fact that you wanna get
your kids out off the technology

00:23:17.080 --> 00:23:19.000
and out into the world
during the pandemic,

00:23:19.000 --> 00:23:21.920
the fact that you had cancer
and were going through this,

00:23:21.920 --> 00:23:24.590
but chose to spend your time
doing and focusing on this,

00:23:24.590 --> 00:23:26.440
you are the example.

00:23:26.440 --> 00:23:28.930
- Well, thank you, Drew,
(clapping) thank you!

00:23:28.930 --> 00:23:30.380
- It's true.
- I wanna be.

00:23:30.380 --> 00:23:32.440
- You are, what's next for you?

00:23:32.440 --> 00:23:35.080
What else are we gonna learn from you?

00:23:35.080 --> 00:23:39.060
- Well, I'm gonna go race this 2021,

00:23:39.060 --> 00:23:42.136
and this year, I'm gonna win.

00:23:42.136 --> 00:23:44.189
(audience cheers)
So those are my goals,

00:23:44.189 --> 00:23:47.750
to race and to win in 2021.

00:23:47.750 --> 00:23:50.950
- [Drew] Well, you are the biggest winner,

00:23:50.950 --> 00:23:52.660
and we wanna be cheering you on,

00:23:52.660 --> 00:23:54.890
and I have a little something for you.

00:23:54.890 --> 00:23:57.763
- Oh, really, for me?
- Yeah, this is a little-

00:23:57.763 --> 00:23:59.840
- Oh, look, it's got my name on it!

00:23:59.840 --> 00:24:01.610
- Oh, yeah, it does.
(Debra laughs)

00:24:01.610 --> 00:24:02.443
(Debra clapping)
- I hope you don't mind.

00:24:02.443 --> 00:24:05.370
We put a little logo of our show on there.

00:24:05.370 --> 00:24:06.203
Here you go.
- Oh, my goodness,

00:24:06.203 --> 00:24:07.760
that's a racing suit!

00:24:07.760 --> 00:24:09.960
- And it's just perfectly your size,

00:24:09.960 --> 00:24:13.710
and I will say it's sturdy,
but it's also really soft.

00:24:13.710 --> 00:24:16.430
- Oh, my goodness, thank you, Drew!

00:24:16.430 --> 00:24:19.310
- It is such a pleasure,
but that's not all.

00:24:19.310 --> 00:24:20.480
Check this out.

00:24:20.480 --> 00:24:23.560
So we know you live in Indianapolis,

00:24:23.560 --> 00:24:26.900
so we reached out to the Indy 500.

00:24:26.900 --> 00:24:28.410
When they heard about you,

00:24:28.410 --> 00:24:31.090
they wanted to give you
a few things, as well.

00:24:31.090 --> 00:24:33.480
So they wanna have you wave-
- Oh, my goodness.

00:24:33.480 --> 00:24:34.570
the green flag
(Debra gasps)

00:24:34.570 --> 00:24:36.643
for the Indy 500 practice day.

00:24:36.643 --> 00:24:38.402
(audience cheers)
Yeah, that's right.

00:24:38.402 --> 00:24:42.050
- (clapping) Oh, goodness, Drew!

00:24:42.050 --> 00:24:43.310
- [Drew] How cool is that?

00:24:43.310 --> 00:24:45.480
And they also want-
- This is really cool.

00:24:45.480 --> 00:24:48.280
Oh, that just makes me feel so good.

00:24:48.280 --> 00:24:50.770
Thank you.
- Well, they also wanna put

00:24:50.770 --> 00:24:52.970
your soapbox on display

00:24:52.970 --> 00:24:57.090
in their fan area on actual race day

00:24:57.090 --> 00:25:00.060
and host you and all your grandchildren

00:25:00.060 --> 00:25:01.348
on practice day-
- Oh, thank you.

00:25:01.348 --> 00:25:03.100
(audience cheers)
- And show you off

00:25:03.100 --> 00:25:05.023
like a little Debra museum!

00:25:05.862 --> 00:25:08.293
- Thank you so much!

00:25:10.170 --> 00:25:13.390
- Oh, Debra, do you mind
if we speak to you again

00:25:13.390 --> 00:25:17.430
and ask you how that day
went and just check in?

00:25:17.430 --> 00:25:19.623
- Yes, oh, you can.

00:25:21.986 --> 00:25:24.770
Please, please call me, I'll call you!

00:25:24.770 --> 00:25:25.603
- Okay, good, I'm so relieved.
(Debra laughs)

00:25:25.603 --> 00:25:28.110
I'm like, Debra, I need more.

00:25:28.110 --> 00:25:30.980
I wanna catch up and
see how that day went,

00:25:30.980 --> 00:25:35.640
and thank you to the Indy 500

00:25:35.640 --> 00:25:36.840
who gets it-
- Thank you!

00:25:36.840 --> 00:25:40.050
- Wants to honor Debra, we
honor you here at this show.

00:25:40.050 --> 00:25:42.410
We love you, and I can't thank you enough

00:25:42.410 --> 00:25:46.560
for being here to be that example.

00:25:46.560 --> 00:25:48.687
- Well, thank you, Drew,
and thank you for having me,

00:25:48.687 --> 00:25:50.420
and thank you for all of that.

00:25:50.420 --> 00:25:53.051
Thank you so much.
- Oh, thank you, Debra!

00:25:53.051 --> 00:25:55.900
(audience applauds)
Debra is the best,

00:25:55.900 --> 00:25:57.470
and we followed up with her

00:25:57.470 --> 00:26:00.540
after her big day at the Indy
500, and she told us she felt

00:26:00.540 --> 00:26:03.650
like a true celebrity and queen that day.

00:26:03.650 --> 00:26:04.950
And they actually showed

00:26:04.950 --> 00:26:06.990
her "Drew Barrymore Show" appearance

00:26:06.990 --> 00:26:09.740
on the big screens at the race track,

00:26:09.740 --> 00:26:12.850
and she said all the
professional drivers were asking

00:26:12.850 --> 00:26:14.740
to take pictures with her.

00:26:14.740 --> 00:26:17.490
So fun and just so deserved.

00:26:17.490 --> 00:26:19.960
We're rooting for you, Debra.

00:26:19.960 --> 00:26:23.450
More behind the scenes
in just a minute, okay?

00:26:23.450 --> 00:26:25.419
We'll see you in a second,
hopefully, all right, bye.

00:26:25.419 --> 00:26:30.419
(upbeat music)
(audience cheers)

00:26:35.375 --> 00:26:39.270
(upbeat music)
(audience applauds)

00:26:39.270 --> 00:26:41.260
Welcome back, do you ever watch our show

00:26:41.260 --> 00:26:45.250
and wonder what happens after
the cameras stop rolling?

00:26:45.250 --> 00:26:48.010
Well, all week long, we're revisiting

00:26:48.010 --> 00:26:50.230
some of our favorite Season One moments

00:26:50.230 --> 00:26:53.373
and sharing behind-the-scenes
bonus commentary.

00:26:55.371 --> 00:26:58.470
I don't know if you know,
but I am a beauty junkie,

00:26:58.470 --> 00:27:00.380
so I always look forward

00:27:00.380 --> 00:27:02.570
to our segment called Beauty in a Box,

00:27:02.570 --> 00:27:05.320
where I get to customize
the perfect beauty routine

00:27:05.320 --> 00:27:08.870
for one of you and send
it right to your door

00:27:08.870 --> 00:27:11.430
in a care package and
then take you through it.

00:27:11.430 --> 00:27:14.250
And our first-ever Beauty
in a Box segment was

00:27:14.250 --> 00:27:17.400
with a viewer named
Daniella who wrote to us

00:27:17.400 --> 00:27:20.920
with a very relatable beauty dilemma.

00:27:20.920 --> 00:27:22.023
Take a look.

00:27:23.330 --> 00:27:24.930
- Hi, Drew, my name is Daniella.

00:27:24.930 --> 00:27:26.200
I'm 40 years old.

00:27:26.200 --> 00:27:27.760
I live in Illinois.

00:27:27.760 --> 00:27:31.100
I am a working mom with four kids.

00:27:31.100 --> 00:27:32.680
I need some help with makeup.

00:27:32.680 --> 00:27:35.100
I need a five-minute routine

00:27:35.100 --> 00:27:38.730
that will enhance the most features,

00:27:38.730 --> 00:27:42.030
'cause five minutes is
about as much time as I have

00:27:42.030 --> 00:27:43.800
with four kids and working.

00:27:43.800 --> 00:27:46.010
Also, if you could help me with mascara,

00:27:46.010 --> 00:27:48.320
I hate putting it on, it smudges,

00:27:48.320 --> 00:27:50.340
and I look like a raccoon within an hour.

00:27:50.340 --> 00:27:52.310
It's just underneath my eyes.

00:27:52.310 --> 00:27:56.080
So if I have to wear it,
please teach me how to use it.

00:27:56.080 --> 00:27:58.940
Thank you, and I really need your help.

00:27:58.940 --> 00:28:01.010
(audience applauds)

00:28:01.010 --> 00:28:05.330
- Daniella, I have to tell
you, you are so beautiful.

00:28:05.330 --> 00:28:06.830
I've seen your video before,

00:28:06.830 --> 00:28:10.930
but as I'm rewatching it, I'm
just like, you're so pretty.

00:28:10.930 --> 00:28:11.763
- Thank you! (laughing)

00:28:11.763 --> 00:28:16.080
That's a very big compliment
coming from Drew Barrymore!

00:28:16.080 --> 00:28:18.500
- Well, what I put together for you,

00:28:18.500 --> 00:28:20.320
do you have a box in front of you?

00:28:20.320 --> 00:28:23.088
We sent you some beauty products.

00:28:23.088 --> 00:28:25.583
(cheers) All right.
- I do. (laughs)

00:28:25.583 --> 00:28:27.950
- This is Beauty in a Box.

00:28:27.950 --> 00:28:29.850
Shall we open it together?

00:28:29.850 --> 00:28:31.690
- Yes, please.
- Okay.

00:28:31.690 --> 00:28:36.690
So what I got for you first
is, I love the company Kiehl's,

00:28:37.130 --> 00:28:42.130
and this is a Skin Tone
and Beautifying BB Cream,

00:28:42.140 --> 00:28:43.800
but it also has sunscreen.

00:28:43.800 --> 00:28:45.250
Do you wear sunscreen?

00:28:45.250 --> 00:28:46.590
- I do, that's probably the only thing

00:28:46.590 --> 00:28:48.300
that I'm very consistent about. (laughs)

00:28:48.300 --> 00:28:50.610
- Oh, my God, I'm so proud
of you and happy for you

00:28:50.610 --> 00:28:51.880
because I'm terrible about it.

00:28:51.880 --> 00:28:54.980
Unless I'm going into
the sun, I always forget.

00:28:54.980 --> 00:28:59.370
So tinted moisturizers and light BB creams

00:28:59.370 --> 00:29:01.740
with sunscreen are just
great for daily wear,

00:29:01.740 --> 00:29:03.960
and they're gonna be a really light layer.

00:29:03.960 --> 00:29:08.550
You can literally put it into
your hands like a moisturizer

00:29:08.550 --> 00:29:11.030
and then do the pat, pat, pat,

00:29:11.030 --> 00:29:13.180
and then you'll go under the eyes,

00:29:13.180 --> 00:29:15.690
and you can always add more.

00:29:15.690 --> 00:29:17.770
You look amazing!
- This feels really nice.

00:29:17.770 --> 00:29:21.560
- Wow!
- That's crazy! (laughs)

00:29:21.560 --> 00:29:22.393
- Okay, (clapping) I am

00:29:22.393 --> 00:29:24.570
so pleased.
- That's already different.

00:29:24.570 --> 00:29:25.990
- What do you think, do you like it?

00:29:25.990 --> 00:29:28.590
- Well, it's nice because it's light.

00:29:28.590 --> 00:29:30.130
It feels really nice on.

00:29:30.130 --> 00:29:32.770
It's very moisturizing.
- Okay.

00:29:32.770 --> 00:29:34.570
Now next, what I got you,

00:29:34.570 --> 00:29:38.190
this is a company called
AMAZING, AMAZINGCONCEALER,

00:29:38.190 --> 00:29:41.840
and this is for if you ever
have more sleepless nights

00:29:41.840 --> 00:29:44.640
or you're just a little more
exhausted or you get a blemish,

00:29:44.640 --> 00:29:49.450
and what's nice is that the
pigment is nice and heavy,

00:29:49.450 --> 00:29:52.660
so it'll cover up dark circles or a spot,

00:29:52.660 --> 00:29:55.820
but it's very blendable on the edges.

00:29:55.820 --> 00:29:58.250
Otherwise, you're gonna see the circle.

00:29:58.250 --> 00:29:59.110
Under my eyes?
- Yeah,

00:29:59.110 --> 00:30:00.690
just a teeny dot, dot, dot,

00:30:00.690 --> 00:30:04.000
and then you can work it in
with your fingers, very minimal.

00:30:04.000 --> 00:30:06.530
This is for those Cryptkeeper days

00:30:06.530 --> 00:30:08.960
when the kids have exhausted you.

00:30:08.960 --> 00:30:12.050
Oh, my God, you look so
beautiful, I'm so excited!

00:30:12.050 --> 00:30:14.410
I swear, I feel like, I don't know.

00:30:14.410 --> 00:30:18.200
I feel like an artist right
now and like I'm painting you,

00:30:18.200 --> 00:30:20.939
and I'm like, look at this, a
painting, she's so beautiful!

00:30:20.939 --> 00:30:22.820
(audience laughs)
Oh, my God,

00:30:22.820 --> 00:30:26.260
I'm so happy right now, 'cause
you were already so beautiful

00:30:26.260 --> 00:30:28.770
and I want things that will not take away

00:30:28.770 --> 00:30:30.190
from your natural beauty.

00:30:30.190 --> 00:30:33.270
Okay, this one is actually
from FLOWER Beauty.

00:30:33.270 --> 00:30:36.840
It's called Gel Crush, and
the reason I love this,

00:30:36.840 --> 00:30:39.100
it's brand new for our company.

00:30:39.100 --> 00:30:41.170
You take it off, it's great for the bag.

00:30:41.170 --> 00:30:43.280
I also love a good purse-friendly makeup.

00:30:43.280 --> 00:30:45.210
When you have a foundation
the size of this,

00:30:45.210 --> 00:30:47.270
you're probably not
throwing it in your purse.

00:30:47.270 --> 00:30:50.060
So this is dot, dot, dot,

00:30:50.060 --> 00:30:53.940
dot, dot, dot and a
little smudge on the lips,

00:30:53.940 --> 00:30:56.340
just so if you want a pop of color,

00:30:56.340 --> 00:30:58.760
you know you can get it out of this.

00:30:58.760 --> 00:31:02.480
Oh, Daniella, you are looking so foxy!

00:31:02.480 --> 00:31:06.281
I'm so pleased right now, I
feel like a proud peacock.

00:31:06.281 --> 00:31:08.462
(audience laughs)
- Is it too much or no?

00:31:08.462 --> 00:31:10.420
- No, not at all, that's great,

00:31:10.420 --> 00:31:12.693
and then work it all over the lips,

00:31:13.996 --> 00:31:15.500
like a deodorant fell in love

00:31:15.500 --> 00:31:16.597
with a lipstick and had a baby.

00:31:16.597 --> 00:31:19.160
(Daniella laughs)
(audience laughs)

00:31:19.160 --> 00:31:22.010
Yes, oh, that just gave
that perfect little kick,

00:31:22.010 --> 00:31:24.720
where it picks up your natural pigment.

00:31:24.720 --> 00:31:26.867
The thing that I care the most
about with FLOWER Beauty is

00:31:26.867 --> 00:31:29.220
that it will never leave a woman hanging.

00:31:29.220 --> 00:31:30.950
When we have a formula,

00:31:30.950 --> 00:31:33.850
it never gathers or goes in the cracks.

00:31:33.850 --> 00:31:36.930
The pigment just goes
away, the hydration stays.

00:31:36.930 --> 00:31:41.260
Okay, next from FLOWER, I
got you our Lash Warrior,

00:31:41.260 --> 00:31:43.120
and the reason I love this is

00:31:43.120 --> 00:31:45.630
it looks like a weapon because it is.

00:31:45.630 --> 00:31:48.010
It is an amazing mascara,

00:31:48.010 --> 00:31:51.910
and it actually has a rubber wand,

00:31:51.910 --> 00:31:54.660
which is gonna distribute
through the lash differently

00:31:54.660 --> 00:31:57.690
and it's gonna lead to less flakeage.

00:31:57.690 --> 00:32:00.410
I think you're doing a phenomenal job.

00:32:00.410 --> 00:32:03.800
Okay, now at the end,
I put this in special.

00:32:03.800 --> 00:32:05.120
This is micellar water.

00:32:05.120 --> 00:32:06.310
I discovered this

00:32:06.310 --> 00:32:08.520
because all the people
in the fashion industry

00:32:08.520 --> 00:32:11.040
for the runway fashion
shows were using this,

00:32:11.040 --> 00:32:13.660
'cause they could take off all
the makeup in one fell swoop.

00:32:13.660 --> 00:32:16.050
And it used to only be
available in France,

00:32:16.050 --> 00:32:19.550
and now micellar waters
are always on trend.

00:32:19.550 --> 00:32:20.990
So this is a Garnier.

00:32:20.990 --> 00:32:23.340
You can find this anywhere.

00:32:23.340 --> 00:32:25.090
So when you're done with all of this,

00:32:25.090 --> 00:32:27.550
you wanna put this on the pad

00:32:27.550 --> 00:32:30.070
and you wanna just take everything off

00:32:30.070 --> 00:32:31.880
and make it nice and clean and clear.

00:32:31.880 --> 00:32:36.130
No matter what you do, do not
go to bed with your makeup on.

00:32:36.130 --> 00:32:37.450
- No, it's usually pretty easy,

00:32:37.450 --> 00:32:38.789
'cause I normally don't wear makeup,

00:32:38.789 --> 00:32:41.290
(laughs) but no, I do wash.

00:32:41.290 --> 00:32:42.744
I do have a good cleansing routine.

00:32:42.744 --> 00:32:45.880
It's just the makeup, I
have a hard time with it,

00:32:45.880 --> 00:32:48.540
but this is something I
can totally do on my own

00:32:48.540 --> 00:32:51.720
and quick with four
kids, thank you so much.

00:32:51.720 --> 00:32:53.710
- That's exactly the point,
(audience applauds)

00:32:53.710 --> 00:32:57.360
natural, fast, and absolutely beautiful.

00:32:57.360 --> 00:33:00.160
You already were, and
this just enhances that,

00:33:00.160 --> 00:33:04.510
and really, the whole point
of beauty is how you feel.

00:33:04.510 --> 00:33:08.930
And if something happens where
it boosts the way you feel,

00:33:08.930 --> 00:33:12.100
that is the whole point,
as far as I'm concerned.

00:33:12.100 --> 00:33:13.130
- Thank you so much.

00:33:13.130 --> 00:33:15.750
This was great, I feel great.
(audience applauds)

00:33:15.750 --> 00:33:18.640
- Yay, Daniella, and you,
please keep writing us

00:33:18.640 --> 00:33:21.130
with your beauty dilemmas
because we'll be sending out

00:33:21.130 --> 00:33:25.210
more beauty boxes in Season
Two and I cannot wait.

00:33:25.210 --> 00:33:28.220
Let me be your personal beauty junkie!

00:33:28.220 --> 00:33:29.900
All right, more fun from Season One

00:33:29.900 --> 00:33:31.860
in just a second, as they say.

00:33:31.860 --> 00:33:33.764
Stay right there, we'll be right back.

00:33:33.764 --> 00:33:38.764
(upbeat music)
(audience cheers)

00:33:42.390 --> 00:33:46.210
(upbeat music)
(audience cheers)

00:33:46.210 --> 00:33:47.780
Welcome back, we're getting ready

00:33:47.780 --> 00:33:50.130
for our Season Two premiere next week

00:33:50.130 --> 00:33:52.410
by looking back on some
of our favorite moments

00:33:52.410 --> 00:33:56.930
from Season One, with
some fun bonus facts.

00:33:56.930 --> 00:34:00.270
As a business owner
myself, I am so passionate

00:34:00.270 --> 00:34:02.800
about highlighting
inspiring entrepreneurs,

00:34:02.800 --> 00:34:06.270
and when we heard about Cindy Tawiah,

00:34:06.270 --> 00:34:08.540
we knew that we had to talk to her.

00:34:08.540 --> 00:34:11.560
She is a beauty brand founder who launched

00:34:11.560 --> 00:34:15.300
the first-ever natural
haircare vending machines

00:34:15.300 --> 00:34:18.140
in the U.S., and her genius idea

00:34:18.140 --> 00:34:20.950
to put her products in
a vending machine came

00:34:20.950 --> 00:34:24.790
as a result of a disappointing
setback that she faced.

00:34:24.790 --> 00:34:26.330
Talk about ingenuity.

00:34:26.330 --> 00:34:29.790
I do believe that failure
can lead to success,

00:34:29.790 --> 00:34:32.610
and there is no success without failure.

00:34:32.610 --> 00:34:34.720
Check out our conversation with Cindy

00:34:34.720 --> 00:34:38.990
and the special surprise
that we had in store for her.

00:34:38.990 --> 00:34:40.990
Please welcome Cindy Tawiah!

00:34:40.990 --> 00:34:41.823
(audience cheers)
- Hi, Cindy!

00:34:45.370 --> 00:34:48.660
- Hi, Drew, hi, Ross!
- Hi, (laughs) oh, my God.

00:34:48.660 --> 00:34:50.905
You're cute, I just gotta tell you.

00:34:50.905 --> 00:34:52.976
- Oh, thank you! (exclaims)

00:34:52.976 --> 00:34:55.380
(Ross laughs)
- Your products are

00:34:55.380 --> 00:35:00.110
in Sally's Beauty
Supplies and walmart.com,

00:35:00.110 --> 00:35:02.260
and so are we at FLOWER Beauty,

00:35:02.260 --> 00:35:06.320
so I'm very happy to be
sisters in business with you.

00:35:06.320 --> 00:35:08.720
- Aw, thank you, Drew.

00:35:08.720 --> 00:35:10.550
- [Drew] I've looked into
getting a vending machine,

00:35:10.550 --> 00:35:12.350
and it is no easy feat!

00:35:12.350 --> 00:35:13.680
- Oh, my goodness, Drew.

00:35:13.680 --> 00:35:18.680
Well, I had a wonderful,
successful, thriving, booming store

00:35:18.760 --> 00:35:21.840
at BWI Airport, and I put that store there

00:35:21.840 --> 00:35:25.440
because TSA takes away
all our haircare products,

00:35:25.440 --> 00:35:27.193
and it's so traumatic.

00:35:28.319 --> 00:35:29.282
- Oh, my God.
- I know you've been

00:35:29.282 --> 00:35:30.610
through it, sister girl.
- Yeah, when you go through,

00:35:30.610 --> 00:35:32.057
they look at the ends and they're like,

00:35:32.057 --> 00:35:33.134
"You can't take this through."

00:35:33.134 --> 00:35:34.354
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:35:34.354 --> 00:35:37.850
- Yes, so I opened the store,
everything was going great,

00:35:37.850 --> 00:35:40.380
and then one day, they took away my store.

00:35:40.380 --> 00:35:44.220
It was like, "We're reclaiming the space,"

00:35:44.220 --> 00:35:45.540
and I was devastated.

00:35:45.540 --> 00:35:47.410
I had to lay everybody off

00:35:47.410 --> 00:35:51.310
and literally close my
store, and you know what?

00:35:51.310 --> 00:35:53.130
A girl's gotta get on her feet.

00:35:53.130 --> 00:35:56.360
After a few months, I went
right back to that airport,

00:35:56.360 --> 00:35:58.670
met with the CEO, Mr. Ricky,

00:35:58.670 --> 00:36:00.683
put my PowerPoint presentation
in his face, and I said,

00:36:00.683 --> 00:36:03.930
"This is what I wanna bring
here," and he looked at me.

00:36:03.930 --> 00:36:06.437
He said, "Young lady,
you're very persistent.

00:36:06.437 --> 00:36:07.737
"How many airports do you want?

00:36:07.737 --> 00:36:08.874
"How many concourses do you want?"

00:36:08.874 --> 00:36:11.100
I said, "That's it, amen, we're in."

00:36:11.100 --> 00:36:12.290
(Ross laughs)
So that's

00:36:12.290 --> 00:36:13.520
how that all started.
(everyone applauds)

00:36:13.520 --> 00:36:14.934
- I love that!
- And I did my research

00:36:14.934 --> 00:36:18.530
and engineered it, but girls
have gotta get creative.

00:36:18.530 --> 00:36:19.740
They take away from you,

00:36:19.740 --> 00:36:21.400
you gotta figure out how to bring it back.

00:36:21.400 --> 00:36:22.850
- Yeah, you gotta pivot

00:36:22.850 --> 00:36:24.050
if you wanna be successful.
(Cindy laughs)

00:36:24.050 --> 00:36:25.210
And I know your business-
- That's right!

00:36:25.210 --> 00:36:26.250
- It is successful-
- Pivot!

00:36:26.250 --> 00:36:29.650
- And a core part of it is
not only providing products

00:36:29.650 --> 00:36:32.610
for women, but taking
care of women, as well.

00:36:32.610 --> 00:36:34.090
Why is that important to you?

00:36:34.090 --> 00:36:36.810
- Oh my God, Ross, I'm a
survivor of domestic violence,

00:36:36.810 --> 00:36:39.380
but one of the things that's
very, very important is

00:36:39.380 --> 00:36:42.830
we donate 10% of our proceeds
to homeless shelters,

00:36:42.830 --> 00:36:44.580
and then we do beauty makeovers.

00:36:44.580 --> 00:36:45.940
It's called the Diva Project,

00:36:45.940 --> 00:36:48.340
where we go out and we give
them a full beauty makeover,

00:36:48.340 --> 00:36:51.930
and it's so important for us
to give back to our community,

00:36:51.930 --> 00:36:54.862
and especially women who
are hurting and broken.

00:36:54.862 --> 00:36:57.653
(audience applauds)
- Right, I mean, I'm done.

00:36:58.667 --> 00:37:02.120
(claps) I love you.

00:37:02.120 --> 00:37:04.350
- I just have so much admiration for you,

00:37:04.350 --> 00:37:05.335
I don't know where to begin.

00:37:05.335 --> 00:37:09.930
- Aw, thank you so much, and I you,

00:37:09.930 --> 00:37:12.400
because sisters have to
take care of sisters.

00:37:12.400 --> 00:37:15.410
Women have to pour into each other

00:37:15.410 --> 00:37:17.350
instead of tearing each other down.

00:37:17.350 --> 00:37:20.410
We have to build each other
up, that's how we rise.

00:37:20.410 --> 00:37:21.540
- Well, you're such a caretaker.

00:37:21.540 --> 00:37:23.610
I mean, you weren't always in
the beauty industry, right?

00:37:23.610 --> 00:37:25.610
You were a nurse for 13 years.

00:37:25.610 --> 00:37:28.140
- Yes, I was a nurse for 13 years,

00:37:28.140 --> 00:37:33.130
and what led me to this point
was I had a chemistry teacher

00:37:33.130 --> 00:37:36.290
who taught me how to make
nail polish and lipstick

00:37:36.290 --> 00:37:39.490
when I was 16 years old
in Ghana, West Africa.

00:37:39.490 --> 00:37:43.890
This teacher, Mr. Ofei, he
saw that I was struggling,

00:37:43.890 --> 00:37:45.285
and instead of giving me another F,

00:37:45.285 --> 00:37:47.050
(laughing) which I had
been getting, by the way,

00:37:47.050 --> 00:37:48.321
(Ross laughs)
he said, "Young lady,

00:37:48.321 --> 00:37:50.423
"I'm gonna teach you how to
make nail polish and lipstick,

00:37:50.423 --> 00:37:52.530
"and you're gonna learn to love my class,"

00:37:52.530 --> 00:37:54.000
and then when he was done,

00:37:54.000 --> 00:37:56.610
he had me be part of the science fair.

00:37:56.610 --> 00:37:58.880
That was for the bright,
intelligent students,

00:37:58.880 --> 00:38:00.550
not for dodos like me.

00:38:00.550 --> 00:38:03.004
So of course, at the science
fair, he presented me

00:38:03.004 --> 00:38:05.167
as a cosmetologist and a
chemist, and I thought,

00:38:05.167 --> 00:38:08.090
"Oh, my God, that's what I
wanna be when I grow up."

00:38:08.090 --> 00:38:09.320
I went home and told my daddy.

00:38:09.320 --> 00:38:11.877
He said, "No, you are going
into the medical field.

00:38:11.877 --> 00:38:13.927
"I didn't send you to school

00:38:13.927 --> 00:38:16.310
"so that you could go
and do the beauty thing,"

00:38:16.310 --> 00:38:17.460
and I thought, "Wow."

00:38:17.460 --> 00:38:20.450
So fear shot me down, I stayed in nursing,

00:38:20.450 --> 00:38:23.070
and 13 years later, I got my wings!

00:38:23.070 --> 00:38:26.250
I got my courage and I left nursing

00:38:26.250 --> 00:38:28.460
to pursue my passion and my purpose,

00:38:28.460 --> 00:38:29.820
and that's why I'm here today.

00:38:29.820 --> 00:38:33.120
I had to change my focus
to change my future.

00:38:33.120 --> 00:38:33.986
- Wow. (claps)
(Drew claps)

00:38:33.986 --> 00:38:35.618
(audience cheers)
- I love that!

00:38:35.618 --> 00:38:39.480
- Actually, Mr. Ofei has

00:38:39.480 --> 00:38:41.960
a message for you.

00:38:41.960 --> 00:38:43.760
Go ahead and roll the clip, please.

00:38:43.760 --> 00:38:48.360
- Hi, Cindy, I'm very proud of you

00:38:48.360 --> 00:38:49.810
and all your accomplishments.

00:38:51.195 --> 00:38:52.120
- God!
- And I do hope

00:38:52.120 --> 00:38:55.360
that you continue to be an inspiration

00:38:55.360 --> 00:38:56.820
for all young girls-
- Oh, my God!

00:38:56.820 --> 00:39:00.730
- Around the world and
continue to inspire them

00:39:00.730 --> 00:39:03.990
to achieve their goals.
(Cindy crying)

00:39:03.990 --> 00:39:06.208
Congratulations.
(audience applauding)

00:39:06.208 --> 00:39:07.458
- Thank you!, oh, my God!

00:39:08.865 --> 00:39:09.782
Oh, my God!

00:39:11.960 --> 00:39:13.973
I'm sorry, oh, my God!

00:39:15.998 --> 00:39:20.558
He saved my life and the
lives of so many other women!

00:39:20.558 --> 00:39:25.120
Oh, my God, thank you,
Drew, he saved my life,

00:39:25.120 --> 00:39:28.193
and because of him, so many
women have been touched

00:39:28.193 --> 00:39:32.570
because of one person
having faith in another.

00:39:32.570 --> 00:39:34.607
I'm sorry, oh, my God!

00:39:34.607 --> 00:39:36.430
- Don't be sorry!

00:39:36.430 --> 00:39:38.650
I feel like such a lucky fly on the wall

00:39:38.650 --> 00:39:40.929
of this moment that you so deserve.

00:39:40.929 --> 00:39:43.669
- Oh, my God!

00:39:43.669 --> 00:39:46.600
- (laughs) Aw!
- Drew, thank you!

00:39:46.600 --> 00:39:50.460
- Cindy, I just can't wait
to see what you do next,

00:39:50.460 --> 00:39:54.520
and please, let's stay friends
and in touch and continue

00:39:54.520 --> 00:39:58.390
to shine a light on
everything that you're doing,

00:39:58.390 --> 00:40:01.510
because I just think the world
of you, and you can check out

00:40:01.510 --> 00:40:04.890
her products online at divabycindy.com.

00:40:04.890 --> 00:40:06.526
And thank you for being on the show.

00:40:06.526 --> 00:40:07.526
(audience cheers)
Thank you.

00:40:07.526 --> 00:40:09.278
- (claps) So proud of you.
- Thank you so much, Drew.

00:40:09.278 --> 00:40:11.177
Thank you so, so much,

00:40:11.177 --> 00:40:13.127
and I would definitely
love to connect with you

00:40:13.127 --> 00:40:15.980
and help you with your vending
machine, I'm here for you.

00:40:15.980 --> 00:40:16.813
- Great!
- Yeah, I need-

00:40:16.813 --> 00:40:17.800
- Yes.
- Your guidance,

00:40:17.800 --> 00:40:20.870
'cause I totally couldn't pull
it off, thank you so much.

00:40:20.870 --> 00:40:21.730
I think you have a lot

00:40:21.730 --> 00:40:22.699
to teach me, Cindy.
- I'm available!

00:40:22.699 --> 00:40:25.910
(audience applauds)
- What an inspirational,

00:40:25.910 --> 00:40:28.270
wonderful, awesome woman.

00:40:28.270 --> 00:40:32.470
We chatted with Cindy recently,
and she has not slowed down.

00:40:32.470 --> 00:40:34.630
She launched one of her vending machines

00:40:34.630 --> 00:40:37.180
on a military base in Virginia,

00:40:37.180 --> 00:40:42.180
and Mr. Ofei has asked her to
mentor some of his students.

00:40:42.710 --> 00:40:46.010
I love this, we'll be right
back to spill some more secrets

00:40:46.010 --> 00:40:47.812
about Season Two, don't go anywhere.

00:40:47.812 --> 00:40:48.770
(upbeat music)
We're gonna spill.

00:40:48.770 --> 00:40:52.520
